@using AuthWithAdmin.Shared.AuthSharedModels

@* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   StudentDashboardHero — how the Dashboard opens.

     1. an h1 greeting sitting directly on the canvas
     2. a "מסע הפרויקט" section card holding the PHASE STRIP

   ── WHY A PHASE STRIP AND NOT THE STEPPER ────────────────────
   This project has fourteen milestones. Rendered as fourteen equally
   prominent stepper stages they are a wall of 12px labels that answers
   none of the three questions a student opens a dashboard with — where
   am I, what is next, how much is left — and costs ~135px of the fold
   to not answer them.

   So the dashboard now shows the journey GROUPED, at most four bands:

       הושלמו · בעבודה עכשיו · הבא בתור · בהמשך

   Each band is a run of the SAME milestones, in the same order, under
   a name that describes the run rather than one invented for it. A band
   with no milestones is not rendered, so a project that has not started
   shows two bands and one that is finished shows one.

   ── NOTHING IS HIDDEN, AND NOTHING IS SUMMARISED AWAY ────────
   A band expands IN PLACE to its own milestones, and every row still
   calls OnOpenMilestone — the same callback the stepper's dots called,
   opening the same MilestoneDetailModal with the same milestone. The
   full fourteen-stage stepper is untouched and still renders on
   /project and inside the milestone modal, which is where a stage-by-
   stage reading belongs. This screen is the summary; that one is the
   detail.

   ── WHY NOT THE PRODUCT'S OWN SEVEN STAGES ───────────────────
   Gradify HAS a real phase concept — RoadmapStages ("בחירה ושיבוצים",
   "התנעה", "אפיון", …), and this cycle's milestones are fully bound to
   it. It would be the better grouping and it is deliberately NOT used:
   every roadmap endpoint is [Authorize(Admin, Staff, Mentor)] and
   MilestoneSummaryDto carries no stage id, so reaching it from a
   student session needs a permission or DTO change — which this pass is
   explicitly not allowed to make. Rather than GUESS at stage boundaries
   from dates (they do not line up: one אפיון milestone falls due after
   a פיתוח one), the bands are derived from state, which is a fact this
   payload already carries. Swap the source, keep the strip, if the
   endpoint is ever opened to students.

   ── WHY THE BANDS DO NOT READ IsCurrentlyOpen ────────────────
   The stepper's own StateOf calls a milestone active when it is
   IsCurrentlyOpen — inside its visibility window. That is right for a
   stepper, where each stage has its own dot, and useless for banding:
   on live data SIX of this project's fourteen milestones are inside
   their window at once, so every remaining milestone landed in
   "בעבודה עכשיו" and the strip collapsed to two bands with no next.

   "Open for submission" is not "being worked on". So a band's active
   set is the milestone the WHOLE DASHBOARD already calls current —
   StudentDashboardModel.CurrentMilestone, the same pick the focus card
   and /tasks read — plus any milestone that has actually started
   (InProgress / Delayed, or some of its tasks already done). Everything
   still ahead splits into the very next one and the rest.

   Nothing about any milestone's real status changes here, and the
   fourteen-stage stepper on /project still uses its own StateOf,
   untouched, IsCurrentlyOpen and all.
   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@

@* The wrapper is not decoration: scoped-CSS ::deep needs an element that
   belongs to THIS component to hang off, and MPageHeader/MCard are
   components with their own roots. *@
<div class="sdh-open">

    <MPageHeader Variant="MPageHeader.HeaderVariant.Hero"
                 Class="sdh-header"
                 Title="@Greeting" />

@if (Milestones.Count > 0)
{
    <MCard Padding="MCard.CardPadding.Large" Class="sdh-journey">
        @* The mentor dashboard's head — the glyph ALONE (no chip), the
           title at the quiet card's step, the count at the reading end. *@
        <div class="sd-head sdh-journey-heading">
            <span class="sd-head-icon motiva-ico-gradient" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="url(#motivaIconGradient)"
                     stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                    <circle cx="6" cy="19" r="3"></circle>
                    <circle cx="18" cy="5" r="3"></circle>
                    <path d="M9 19h4a5 5 0 0 0 0-10H9"></path>
                </svg>
            </span>
            <h2 class="sd-head-title">מסע הפרויקט</h2>
            <span class="sdh-journey-count">@_completedCount מתוך @Milestones.Count אבני דרך הושלמו</span>
        </div>

        @*
            THE STRIP, in the mentor project workspace's own phase grammar
            (the shared ProjectWorkspace ".pw-stages"): equal-width bands, a
            5px rounded track each, then dot · name · a quiet detail line.
            Same geometry, same four-state colour logic, student content.

            A band's track is SOLID in its state's colour, as the mentor
            draws it. An earlier pass part-filled the active band with its
            own task completion; on real data that fill is often near
            zero, which rendered the one band that matters as the palest
            thing on the strip. The percentage is not lost — it is on
            every milestone inside the band, one click away.
        *@
        <ol class="sdh-phases" style="--sdh-phase-count:@_phases.Count" aria-label="שלבי הפרויקט">
            @foreach (var phase in _phases)
            {
                var p    = phase;
                var open = _openPhase == p.Key;

                <li class="@($"sdh-phase sdh-phase-{p.Key}")">
                    <button type="button"
                            class="sdh-phase-btn"
                            @onclick="@(() => TogglePhase(p.Key))"
                            aria-expanded="@open"
                            aria-controls="@($"sdh-p-{p.Key}")"
                            aria-label="@($"{p.Name} — {p.Count} אבני דרך. פתיחת הרשימה")">

                        <span class="sdh-phase-track" aria-hidden="true"></span>

                        <span class="sdh-phase-name">
                            <span class="sdh-phase-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            <span class="sdh-phase-text" title="@p.Name">@p.Name</span>
                            <span class="sdh-phase-count-chip">@p.Count</span>
                        </span>

                        <span class="sdh-phase-detail" title="@p.Detail">@p.Detail</span>
                    </button>
                </li>
            }
        </ol>

        @*
            The expanded band — opened IN PLACE under the strip, one at a
            time, exactly as the mentor dashboard opens an attention
            group. Every row is a real milestone and still opens THAT
            milestone's own modal.
        *@
        @if (_openPhase is not null && _openMilestones.Count > 0)
        {
            <div class="sdh-phase-items" id="@($"sdh-p-{_openPhase}")">
                @foreach (var ms in _openMilestones)
                {
                    var m = ms;
                    <button type="button"
                            class="sdh-ms-row"
                            @onclick="@(() => OnOpenMilestone.InvokeAsync(m))"
                            aria-label="@($"פתיחת אבן הדרך {m.Title}")">
                        <span class="@($"sdh-ms-dot sdh-ms-dot-{ToneOf(m)}")" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        <span class="sdh-ms-title" title="@m.Title">@m.Title</span>
                        <span class="@(IsPast(m) ? "sdh-ms-due sdh-ms-due-past" : "sdh-ms-due")">@DueText(m)</span>
                    </button>
                }
            </div>
        }
    </MCard>
}

</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public List<MilestoneSummaryDto>          Milestones      { get; set; } = new();
    [Parameter]                 public string?                            FirstName       { get; set; }
    [Parameter]                 public EventCallback<MilestoneSummaryDto> OnOpenMilestone { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The expanded band's key, or null. ONE AT A TIME — a second
    /// click closes the first, which is what keeps the card's height from
    /// running away and is the same rule the mentor dashboard's attention
    /// groups follow. Pure view state: nothing is persisted or sent.</summary>
    private string? _openPhase;

    /// <summary>The bands, rebuilt whenever the milestone list changes rather
    /// than on every access — the strip reads it, the expanded list reads it,
    /// and the aria labels read it.</summary>
    private List<Phase> _phases = new();

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        _phases = BuildPhases();

        // A band the new data no longer has cannot stay open.
        if (_openPhase is not null && _phases.All(p => p.Key != _openPhase))
            _openPhase = null;
    }

    private void TogglePhase(string key) => _openPhase = _openPhase == key ? null : key;

    private List<MilestoneSummaryDto> _openMilestones =>
        _phases.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Key == _openPhase)?.Items ?? new();

    // ── Copy ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    // A time-of-day greeting, not stored data. The name comes from the
    // cascaded user; it renders correctly without one rather than showing an
    // empty comma.
    private string Greeting
    {
        get
        {
            var hour = DateTime.Now.Hour;
            var part = hour < 12 ? "בוקר טוב"
                     : hour < 18 ? "צהריים טובים"
                     : "ערב טוב";
            return string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(FirstName) ? part : $"{part}, {FirstName}";
        }
    }

    private int _completedCount => Milestones.Count(m => m.Status == "Completed");

    // ── The bands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>One band of the strip.</summary>
    private sealed record Phase(
        string Key,
        string Name,
        int    Count,
        string Detail,
        List<MilestoneSummaryDto> Items);

    /// <summary>
    /// The milestone list, grouped — never filtered, never re-sorted, never
    /// re-stated.
    ///
    /// <para>Every milestone lands in exactly one band and the bands are
    /// emitted in journey order, so reading the strip left to right (RTL:
    /// right to left) walks the same sequence the full stepper walks on
    /// /project. A band with nothing in it is not rendered at all, which is
    /// what lets a project that has not started show two bands and a finished
    /// one show a single band, without a special case for either.</para>
    /// </summary>
    private List<Phase> BuildPhases()
    {
        // The dashboard's canonical "where you are". Reading it here is what
        // guarantees the strip and the focus card under it cannot disagree.
        var anchor = StudentDashboardModel.CurrentMilestone(Milestones);

        var done  = new List<MilestoneSummaryDto>();
        var now   = new List<MilestoneSummaryDto>();
        var ahead = new List<MilestoneSummaryDto>();

        foreach (var m in Milestones)
        {
            if (m.Status == "Completed")      done.Add(m);
            else if (IsInWork(m, anchor))     now.Add(m);
            else                              ahead.Add(m);
        }

        // "הבא בתור" is the first one still ahead in the PROJECT'S OWN ORDER,
        // not the earliest by date. The two genuinely differ in live data — a
        // late אפיון milestone can fall due after an early פיתוח one — and the
        // sequence is what /project's stepper draws, so picking by date here
        // would have the two screens disagree about what comes next.
        var next  = ahead.FirstOrDefault();
        var later = ahead.Skip(1).ToList();

        var phases = new List<Phase>();

        if (done.Count > 0)
            phases.Add(new Phase("done", "הושלמו", done.Count,
                                 $"{StudentDashboardModel.OverallPercent(Milestones)}% מהמסע", done));

        if (now.Count > 0)
            phases.Add(new Phase("now", "בעבודה עכשיו", now.Count,
                                 NowDetail(now), now));

        if (next is not null)
            phases.Add(new Phase("next", "הבא בתור", 1,
                                 NextDetail(next),
                                 new List<MilestoneSummaryDto> { next }));

        if (later.Count > 0)
            phases.Add(new Phase("later", "בהמשך", later.Count,
                                 LaterDetail(later), later));

        return phases;
    }

    /// <summary>Whether a milestone is genuinely being worked on: the one the
    /// dashboard calls current, one the data says is InProgress/Delayed, or one
    /// that already has finished tasks in it.
    ///
    /// <para>Deliberately NOT IsCurrentlyOpen — see the header note. Being
    /// inside a visibility window says a milestone CAN be worked on, not that
    /// it is, and six of them are open at once on real data.</para></summary>
    private static bool IsInWork(MilestoneSummaryDto m, MilestoneSummaryDto? anchor) =>
        m.ProjectMilestoneId == anchor?.ProjectMilestoneId
        || m.Status is "InProgress" or "Delayed"
        || (m.Tasks.Count > 0 && m.Tasks.Any(StudentDashboardModel.IsComplete));

    /// <summary>The active band names the milestone the rest of the dashboard
    /// is already built around — StudentDashboardModel.CurrentMilestone, the
    /// same pick the focus card and the tasks page read — so the strip cannot
    /// disagree with the card beneath it about where the project is.</summary>
    private string NowDetail(List<MilestoneSummaryDto> now)
    {
        var primary = StudentDashboardModel.CurrentMilestone(Milestones);
        var lead    = now.FirstOrDefault(m => m.ProjectMilestoneId == primary?.ProjectMilestoneId)
                      ?? now[0];

        return now.Count == 1 ? lead.Title : $"{lead.Title} · ועוד {now.Count - 1}";
    }

    private static string NextDetail(MilestoneSummaryDto m) =>
        m.DueDate is DateTime d ? $"{m.Title} · עד {d:dd.MM}" : m.Title;

    private static string LaterDetail(List<MilestoneSummaryDto> later)
    {
        var last = later.Where(m => m.DueDate.HasValue).Max(m => m.DueDate);
        return last is DateTime d ? $"עד {d:dd.MM}" : "ללא מועד יעד";
    }

    // ── The expanded rows ───────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>A row's dot, in its own band's colour, so an expanded band
    /// reads as part of the band that opened it.</summary>
    private string ToneOf(MilestoneSummaryDto m) =>
        m.Status == "Completed"                                           ? "done"
        : IsInWork(m, StudentDashboardModel.CurrentMilestone(Milestones)) ? "now"
        :                                                                   "later";

    /// <summary>Whether the milestone's own due date has already passed.
    ///
    /// <para>This decides the TONE of a date the row prints either way. It
    /// adds no label, no status and no claim the product does not already
    /// make — it is the same soft rose every other passed date on this
    /// dashboard wears.</para></summary>
    private static bool IsPast(MilestoneSummaryDto m) =>
        m.Status != "Completed" && m.DueDate is DateTime d && d.Date < DateTime.Today;

    private static string DueText(MilestoneSummaryDto m) =>
        m.Status == "Completed"   ? "הושלם"
        : m.DueDate is DateTime d ? $"עד {d:dd.MM}"
        :                           "—";
}
